## 12. Validation and Edge-Case Checklist

The agent must implement and test these, not merely list them.

### Authentication/security
- Wrong email/password.
- Unknown email and incorrect password use a generic error.
- Missing, expired, malformed, or tampered JWT.
- Inactive account.
- Author tries an admin endpoint.
- Author changes `authorId` in the request.
- Author reads another author's book/ticket/message.
- Admin role cannot be assigned by client input.
- Login rate limit.
- CORS rejects unapproved origins.
- Missing or weak production secrets cause startup failure/warning.
- Cookie/session behavior works on the deployed frontend/backend domains.
- No secrets or password hashes in API responses/logs.

### Books/data
- Author with zero books.
- Books in production with no ISBN/publication date/sales/royalty.
- Book with actual zero sales and zero royalties.
- Pending royalty greater than zero and zero paid.
- Missing optional genre/MRP/ISBN.
- Invalid or null dates.
- Unknown status value from source data.
- Very long title or ISBN-like string.
- Currency/number formatting without `NaN` or incorrect symbols.
- Dataset import run twice.
- Dataset contains duplicate/missing IDs or invalid references.
- Sample author-book associations remain correct.

### Ticket creation and reads
- Empty/whitespace subject.
- Empty/whitespace description.
- Excessively long fields.
- Invalid book ID.
- Author selects a book owned by someone else.
- General/account-level ticket with no book.
- Author with no books can still create a general ticket.
- Rapid double submission.
- Network failure after form submission.
- Ticket list with no tickets.
- Ticket list pagination boundary and invalid page/limit.
- Query with unsupported status/category/priority.
- Invalid date range (`from > to`).
- Search text with special characters/regex input.
- Ticket detail requested by non-owner.
- Missing/deleted associated book/author is handled gracefully.

### Ticket management
- Invalid status/category/priority.
- Admin override is retained and marked as manual.
- AI re-run does not silently overwrite manual overrides.
- Assign to self, assign to another valid admin if supported, unassign.
- Assign to a non-admin user is rejected.
- Add an internal note and verify it is never visible to authors.
- Empty internal note rejected.
- Empty public response rejected.
- Double-click send / duplicate network retries.
- Sending a reply does not automatically close the ticket.
- Reopen resolved/closed ticket according to documented behavior.
- Concurrent admin edits do not silently corrupt data; use optimistic concurrency/version checks if practical.
- Audit events identify actor and time.

### AI
- Provider unavailable.
- Request timeout.
- HTTP 429/rate limit.
- Provider 5xx.
- Invalid/malformed structured response.
- Unexpected enum values.
- Prompt injection in ticket body.
- Empty/vague ticket.
- Multiple issues in one ticket.
- Missing account data needed for a definite answer.
- Retry works.
- Manual response still works when AI fails.
- AI draft is not sent until explicit admin action.
- Admin edits the draft before sending.
- Model does not invent royalty dates, amounts, ISBNs, or claim a re-sync/reprint has already been completed.
- Model output and error are not blindly rendered as HTML.
- Cost controls prevent repeated unnecessary model calls.

### Real-time
- Author receives a public response event.
- Author receives allowed status updates if implemented.
- Admin sees ticket changes from another admin.
- Author never receives internal-note content or other authors' events.
- SSE disconnect/reconnect.
- Browser tab sleeps or network switches.
- Event stream authentication works with cookies.
- Event source is closed on logout/unmount.
- Client performs a fresh authorized fetch after reconnect to recover missed events.
- Polling fallback does not cause duplicate messages.

### UI/accessibility
- Loading, empty, success, and error states on every major screen.
- Keyboard navigation and visible focus.
- Labels and validation messages for form fields.
- Mobile/tablet layout.
- Long descriptions wrap safely.
- Buttons disable during submissions.
- Confirmation or undo pattern for consequential operations where practical.
- Clear visual distinction between AI suggestion, manual override, public reply, and internal note.
- No misleading “success” toast before the backend confirms success.

